# Component Patterns

## Component Structure

- **Prefer Server Components** by default
- Add `"use client"` only when necessary:
  - Interactive hooks (useState, useEffect, etc.)
  - Browser APIs (window, document)
  - Event handlers (onClick, onChange)
  - Third-party client-only libraries

```tsx
// Server Component (default)
export default async function TicketList() {
  const tickets = await fetchTickets()
  return <div>{/* ... */}</div>
}

// Client Component (when needed)
'use client'
export function TicketForm() {
  const [title, setTitle] = useState('')
  // ...
}
```

## shadcn/ui Integration

- shadcn is available in devDependencies for component generation
- Components live in `src/components/ui/`
- Customize via Tailwind classes and CSS variables
- Use composition for complex components

```tsx
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { Dialog } from '@/components/ui/dialog'

export function CreateTicketDialog() {
  return (
    <Dialog>
      <DialogTrigger asChild>
        <Button variant="default">New Ticket</Button>
      </DialogTrigger>
      <DialogContent>{/* ... */}</DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  )
}
```

## Component Organization

```
src/
├─ components/
│  ├─ ui/           # shadcn/ui primitives
│  ├─ tickets/      # domain-specific components
│  ├─ auth/
│  ├─ chat/
│  └─ shared/       # reusable app components
├─ app/             # routes and pages
└─ lib/             # utilities, hooks, types
```

## Naming Conventions

- Components: `PascalCase` (e.g., `TicketCard.tsx`)
- Hooks: `useFoo` (e.g., `useTickets.ts`)
- Utilities: `camelCase` (e.g., `formatDate.ts`)
- Types/Interfaces: `PascalCase`, suffix with `Props` for component props

```tsx
interface TicketCardProps {
  ticket: Ticket
  onStatusChange?: (status: string) => void
}

export function TicketCard({ ticket, onStatusChange }: TicketCardProps) {
  // ...
}
```

## Composition Over Inheritance

- Build complex UIs by composing smaller components
- Use `children` prop for flexible layouts
- Prefer render props or hooks for sharing logic

```tsx
// Good: Composition
<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Ticket #{ticket.id}</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    {ticket.description}
  </CardContent>
</Card>

// Better: Extract to domain component
<TicketCard ticket={ticket} />
```

## Data Fetching

- **Server Components**: Fetch directly with async/await
- **Client Components**: Use hooks (useState + useEffect or SWR/React Query)
- Prefer streaming and Suspense for progressive loading
- Use Next.js caching strategies (`fetch` options, `revalidate`)

```tsx
// Server Component with fetch
export default async function TicketsPage() {
  const tickets = await fetchTickets() // direct DB or API call
  return <TicketList tickets={tickets} />
}

// With Suspense boundary
<Suspense fallback={<TicketListSkeleton />}>
  <TicketList />
</Suspense>
```

## Forms & Actions

- Use Server Actions for mutations
- Validate on server; optionally use client-side validation for UX
- Handle loading and error states
- Show optimistic updates when appropriate

```tsx
'use client'
import { createTicket } from '@/app/actions/tickets'

export function TicketForm() {
  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition()

  async function handleSubmit(formData: FormData) {
    startTransition(async () => {
      const result = await createTicket(formData)
      if (result.success) {
        // handle success
      }
    })
  }

  return (
    <form action={handleSubmit}>
      {/* form fields */}
      <Button type="submit" disabled={isPending}>
        {isPending ? 'Creating...' : 'Create Ticket'}
      </Button>
    </form>
  )
}
```

## Error Boundaries

- Wrap sections in error boundaries for graceful degradation
- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Log errors for monitoring

```tsx
// app/tickets/error.tsx
'use client'
export default function Error({ error, reset }: {
  error: Error
  reset: () => void
}) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Something went wrong!</h2>
      <button onClick={reset}>Try again</button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide ARIA labels for interactive elements
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain color contrast ratios (≥4.5:1 for text)
- Test with screen readers

## Performance

- Lazy load heavy components with `next/dynamic`
- Memoize expensive computations with `useMemo`
- Prevent unnecessary re-renders with `React.memo` and `useCallback`
- Optimize images with `next/image`

```tsx
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'

const HeavyChart = dynamic(() => import('@/components/analytics/Chart'), {
  loading: () => <p>Loading chart...</p>,
  ssr: false
})
```

